# ── Notebooks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prettier has no .ipynb parser ("No parser could be inferred", exit 2), so a
# notebook anywhere in the tree would turn `npm run lint` — and therefore
# verify:fast, and therefore CI — red on a documentation file. Ignored instead.
# docs/THEME_LOGIC.ipynb is generated by docs/theme-logic/build.ps1.
*.ipynb

# ── Sarkari deploy runtime artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
# The pipeline writes these on every single run (telemetry, challans, JSON
# records). They are output, not source. Letting Prettier check them meant
# `npm run lint` failed permanently for every agent - one of the quiet ways a
# build gets stuck before it has even started.
sarkari_deploy/records/

# ── Sarkari open-contribute drafts ─────────────────────────────────────────
# These are review sketches, written in the language of the file they propose
# to change: PowerShell guards, Rust sketches, Go sketches. Prettier has no
# parser for .ps1 / .rs / .go, so `prettier --check .` aborted with "No parser
# could be inferred" and turned `npm run lint` - and therefore verify:fast -
# red for every agent. The proposals themselves (.md) stay checked.
sarkari_open_contribute/drafts/

